{% comment %}
  Half vertical — 400x480 on an OG. Width is the constraint here, not height:
  the panel is as tall as the full view, so all six rows still fit. What has
  to go is the LO/HI column. The end dot stays: it is a <circle> in the
  unscaled outer svg, so the viewBox squashing x by ~0.55 cannot turn it into
  an ellipse (see shared.liquid).
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
    THE TYPE SCALE
    The pair is `value--xxsmall`, the framework's 16px bitmap tier on a 1-bit
    panel, and the rate `value--xsmall` (20px Inter): the smallest pair of
    tiers that still reads as pair-then-rate. The change is a plain `label`
    pill. A TRMNL X steps each up one (`lg:value--xsmall`, `lg:value--small`,
    `lg:label--large`), which is what fills its panel: at the OG tiers the X
    rendered this view as a strip of small type beside oversized traces.
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    Every pair is exactly XXX -> XXX, so the first column's width is fixed and
    predictable. Declared rather than letting the text overflow a narrower
    track into the gap; the X tracks are measured to the larger tiers.
  {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} Row inset is py--4 (16px) on the row: 17px would not step. {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} TREND is the last column here, so keep the dot's overhang inside it. {% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    No height cap. One existed from the aspect-ratio era, to stop a ratio-driven
    plot going square in this narrow column on a wide panel; with the height
    now derived from the panel it only ever cut the rows short, leaving the
    lower third of a TRMNL X landscape panel empty. Six rows of
    (screen height - chrome) / 6 fill every device.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
    PORTRAIT: TWO LINES PER ROW
    Portrait halves the width again (390px on an X, 240px on an OG), and a
    one-line row left the trace a sliver. So the tracks become `auto auto 1fr`
    for the figures, the trace cell spans all three (`portrait:col--span-3`)
    on a second line, and the TREND header spans the same way. The plot
    height then subtracts that first line (its line box plus the 8px row
    gap) as well as the inset, and the chrome term grows by the header's
    second line; see full.liquid for the terms.
{% endcomment %}
<style>
  .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: 80px minmax(110px, auto) 62px 1fr; gap: 8px; }
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: 112px minmax(142px, auto) 86px 1fr; }
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-row,
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv .fx-head { grid-template-columns: max-content max-content 1fr; }
  .fx--halfv { --fx-top-pad: 10px; --fx-chrome: 82px; --fx-inset: 33px; }
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 90px; }
  .screen--portrait .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 110px; --fx-inset: 70px; }
  .screen--lg.screen--portrait .fx--halfv { --fx-chrome: 98px; --fx-inset: 74px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-dot  { r: 3px; }
  .screen--lg .fx--halfv .fx-dot { r: 4px; }
  .fx--halfv .fx-spark svg { height: calc((var(--screen-h) - var(--fx-chrome) - var(--fx-top-pad)) / 6 - var(--fx-inset)); }
</style>

<div class="layout layout--col layout--justify-start">
  {% if fx_failed %}
    <div class="fx-error flex flex--col flex--center-y text--center">
      <span class="title">Rates unavailable</span>
    </div>
  {% else %}
    <div class="fx-list flex flex--col gap--none pt--2.5 fx--halfv">
      <div class="fx-head grid pb--1">
        <span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base">PAIR</span><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base text--right">LATEST</span><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base text--right">CHANGE</span><span class="label label--small text--bold lg:label--base text--center portrait:col--span-3 portrait:flex--center">{% if range_label %}{{ range_label }} {% endif %}TREND</span>
      </div>

      {% for row in rows limit: 6 %}
        <div class="fx-row grid py--4">
          <div class="fx-pair value value--xxsmall text--bold lg:value--xsmall">{{ row.from }}<span class="fx-arrow text--regular px--0.5">&rarr;</span>{{ row.to }}</div>
          <div class="fx-rate value value--xsmall value--tnums text--bold lg:value--small text--right">{{ row.rate_str }}</div>
          <div class="fx-chg flex flex--right gap--none"><span class="label text--bold lg:label--large {% if row.change_pct < 0 %}label--filled{% else %}label--outline{% endif %}">{{ row.change_str }}%</span></div>
          {% assign fx_end = row.points | split: " " | last | split: "," %}
          {% assign fx_end_y = fx_end[1] | times: 100.0 | divided_by: 30 %}
          <div class="fx-spark flex gap--none pr--1 portrait:col--span-3">
            <svg class="fx-plot block" width="100%" height="24">
              <svg class="block" viewBox="0 0 200 30" width="100%" height="100%" preserveAspectRatio="none">
                <polyline points="{{ row.points }}" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
              </svg>
              <circle class="fx-dot" cx="100%" cy="{{ fx_end_y }}%"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<div class="title_bar">
  {{ fx_icon }}
  <span class="title">Exchange Rates{% if env %} ({{ env | upcase }}){% endif %}</span>
  <span class="instance">{% if fx_failed %}No data{% else %}<span class="fx-dates text--default">{{ fx_dates }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
</div>
